<section class="three-tool-knowledge" id="invest-deep-guide">
<h2>Zakat on stocks, shares and cryptocurrency: full calculation guide</h2>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> Zakat on investments is not necessarily <strong>2.5% of everything in a brokerage or crypto account</strong>. For shares acquired for resale, contemporary guidance often assesses the current full market value. Long-term shares may instead require a portion of underlying qualifying business assets. Cryptocurrencies can be currency-like, trading assets or other rights whose treatment needs careful review. See <a href="https://www.islamic-relief.org.uk/giving/islamic-giving/zakat/zakat-and-investment/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Islamic Relief UK's scholar-reviewed stocks guidance</a> and its <a href="https://www.islamic-relief.org.uk/giving/islamic-giving/zakat/zakat-and-cryptocurrency/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">cryptocurrency guidance</a>.</p>
